                        <p>The possibilities are listed by Ed Pope: Holdens Directory: Richard
                            Coffee, hat-maker, (1802 and 1805) Spitalfields / George Coffee, (1802)
                            carver and gilder, 181 High Holborn (1805) cook, 182 High Holborn /
                            James Coffey, wine importer, Borough (1805 and 1811) / James Coffey,
                            (1805) The Old Thatched House, 419 Strand / John Coffey, tailor, (1805
                            and 1811) 7, Drake-st, Red Lion-sq / John Coffey, (1811) new dairy, 13,
                            King-st, Soho. All the contacts are within the same year (1808) between
                            June and November, when Godwin is trying to establish the Juvenile
                            Library. </p>
